verwrite. Let's avoid ambiguity\u2014maybe keep distinct targets. Actually let's just be careful.\n\nLet me choose loose pixels whose clamped positions are distinct.\n\nBlock 3x3 at rows 3-5, cols 2-4. Ring rows 2-6, cols 1-5.\n\nActually let's make grid 8 rows x 8 cols.\n\nLoose:\n- (0,3): clamp row to 2, col 3 \u2192 (2,3). Row2 is above block? Block rows 3-5. (2,3) is ring top. Good.\n- (0,0): \u2192 (2,1).\n- (7,1): clamp row 6, col 1 \u2192 (6,1).\n- (4,7): row4, col clamp to 5 \u2192 (4,5).\n- (6,0)? \u2192 (6,1) collision with (7,1). Avoid; use (6,6)? clamp col 5 \u2192 (6,5). Hmm (6,5) is bottom-right corner. Fine, distinct.\n\nWait (7,1) \u2192 (6,1); (6,6) \u2192 (6,5). Distinct.\n\nLet me just pick 4 loose pixels: (0,3),(0,0),(7,1),(4,7).\n\nTargets: (2,3),(2,1),(6,1),(4,5). All distinct, none on block.\n\nNow input grid 8x8 all 0 except block and loose.\n\nRow0: cols 0 and 3 =5 \u2192 [5,0,0,5,0,0,0,0]\nRow1: all 0\nRow2: all 0\nRow3: cols2,3,4 =2 \u2192 [0,0,2,2,2,0,0,0]\nRow4: cols2,3,4=2, col7=5 \u2192 [0,0,2,2,2,0,0,5]\nRow5: cols2,3,4=2 \u2192 [0,0,2,2,2,0,0,0]\nRow6: all 0\nRow7: col1=5 \u2192 [0,5,0,0,0,0,0,0]\n\nCheck block: color2 cells rows3-5 cols2-4, filled 3x3. Good. Color5 cells: (0,0),(0,3),(4,7),(7,1). Are they a filled rectangle? bounding box rows0-7, cols0-7, area 64 \u22604. Not filled. Good.\n\nOutput:\nClear loose, place:\n(0,0)\u2192(2,1)\n(0,3)\u2192(2,3)\n(4,7)\u2192(4,5)\n(7,1)\u2192(6,1)\n\nOutput rows:\nRow0: all 0\nRow1: all 0\nRow2: col1=5, col3=5 \u2192 [0,5,0,5,0,0,0,0]\nRow3: [0,0,2,2,2,0,0,0]\nRow4: col2,3,4=2, col5=5 \u2192 [0,0,2,2,2,5,0,0]\nRow5: [0,0,2,2,2,0,0,0]\nRow6: col1=5 \u2192 [0,5,0,0,0,0,0,0]\nRow7: all 0\n\nPair 2: different block, maybe 2x3 rectangle. Background 0, block color 3 (green) or 2. Let's use color 2 again for block; loose 5. Or vary to reinforce. But rule says red boxes and gray boxes, so block red=2, loose gray=5. Keep consistent.\n\nGrid 10x10 maybe. Block 2x2 at rows 4-5, cols 4-5? Let's do bl